      "answer": "a. The **population** is all 1,500 singers in the choir.\n\nb. The **sample** is the 650 singers seated nearest the front who were surveyed.\n\nc. The **parameter** is the true proportion of all 1,500 choir members who are professional singers.\n\nd. The sample statistic is\n\n$$\\hat p=\\frac{26}{650}=0.04.$$\n\nThus, 4% of the surveyed singers are professionals.\n\ne. This is a **convenience sample**, not a random sample. Singers seated near the front may differ systematically from the rest of the choir, so the estimate may be biased.",
